# CHEST-SUPPORTED ROW

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Chest-Supported Row is a bilateral horizontal pulling exercise performed with the torso supported on an inclined bench.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the safest and most efficient exercises for developing upper-back strength while minimizing spinal loading.

---

# Philosophy

Not every pulling exercise should challenge trunk stability.

Sometimes the objective is to maximize upper-back force production while minimizing unnecessary fatigue elsewhere.

CAS selects the Chest-Supported Row when the athlete requires high-quality horizontal pulling with reduced systemic fatigue.

